import{_ as t,o as i,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 285 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Cases of Plot Kidnapping Setting: Typical Cases of Sacrificing Law for Plot","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 285 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Cases of Plot Kidnapping Setting: Typical Cases of Sacrificing Law for Plot","no":285,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Plot Kidnaps Setting","Sacrificing Law","Case Analysis","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table","90-Glossary","98-Expanded Setting Recommendation List"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0285_模块2-唐罗-剧情绑架设定案例.md","filePath":"en/0285_模块2-唐罗-剧情绑架设定案例.md"}'),o={name:"en/0285_模块2-唐罗-剧情绑架设定案例.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,c,p){return i(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-285-tang-luo-decomposition-cases-of-plot-kidnapping-setting-typical-cases-of-sacrificing-law-for-plot" tabindex="-1">Entry 285 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Cases of Plot Kidnapping Setting: Typical Cases of Sacrificing Law for Plot <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-285-tang-luo-decomposition-cases-of-plot-kidnapping-setting-typical-cases-of-sacrificing-law-for-plot" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 285 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Cases of Plot Kidnapping Setting: Typical Cases of Sacrificing Law for Plot&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 35)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-law-yields-to-plot" tabindex="-1">Introduction: When law yields to plot <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-law-yields-to-plot" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: When law yields to plot&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the law-first axiom expressly states: setting self-consistency over plot convenience, plot must not kidnap setting. This entry uses concrete cases to dissect the typical &quot;sacrificing law for plot&quot; pattern in the Tang-Luo system (and similar web novels). This entry takes the law-first axiom as core. Protagonist uniqueness dependency judgment: <strong>Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal-style civilization</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Plot-kidnaps-setting-caused energy-level waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Law authority损耗</strong>: laws painstakingly built early torn open by one plot need. Law&#39;s prestige is discounted from then on</li><li><strong>Reader trust损耗</strong>: readers discover laws can be overturned by plot, trust in the author drops</li><li><strong>Setting elasticity overdrawn</strong>: every setting kidnapping spends one &quot;elasticity.&quot; Elasticity used too much, settings lose hardness</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-kidnapping-perspective" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Kidnapping Perspective) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-kidnapping-perspective" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Kidnapping Perspective)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Plot-kidnaps-setting-caused narrative regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Iron-law ladder collapse</strong>: the first iron law torn, readers can still forgive; the second torn, readers start doubting; the third torn, readers completely disbelieve. Iron laws collapse in a ladder</li><li><strong>Author self-indulgence</strong>: once discovering &quot;tearing it and no one scolds,&quot; the author grows bolder. Kidnapping changes from occasional to routine</li><li><strong>Late stages unmanageable</strong>: by mid-late, settings are already full of holes, the author can only cover smaller patches with bigger patches</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory thinking behind plot-kidnaps-setting:</p><ul><li><strong>Protagonist halo first</strong>: because the protagonist must win, any law in the way can be torn. The protagonist halo is above all</li><li><strong>Emotion over law</strong>: to thrill readers, the author may sacrifice logic. The thrill is real, logic is a tool</li><li><strong>Readers are consumables</strong>: the author treats readers as emotional consumables, not as respected objects. Readers want thrills, so laws step aside</li></ul><p>Typical kidnapping cases (using Douluo / Shrouding-the-Heavens as examples, compared with Tang-Luo):</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Early Iron Law</th><th>Late Kidnapping</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Douluo</td><td>Hundred-year soul rings scarce</td><td>Hundred-thousand-year soul beasts mass-produced</td></tr><tr><td>Shrouding the Heavens</td><td>Realm ladder strict</td><td>Great Emperor / Red-Dust Immortal stage loses constraint</td></tr><tr><td>Tang-Luo system</td><td>Fierce-realm cap</td><td>Late if it needs new enemies, inevitably &quot;there is one more tier above fierce realm&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Tang-Luo system&#39;s most likely kidnapping points: fierce-realm cap, racial boundaries, top-tier knowledge private — these three once plot needs to break through, are typical &quot;plot kidnaps setting.&quot;</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Plot Kidnaps Setting</th><th>Law First</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Iron laws torn by plot</td><td>Iron laws are laws, not torn</td></tr><tr><td>Protagonist halo first</td><td>Law above protagonist</td></tr><tr><td>Emotion over logic</td><td>Logical self-consistency over thrills</td></tr><tr><td>Readers are consumables</td><td>Readers are contracting parties</td></tr><tr><td>Patches cover patches</td><td>Laws first, no patches</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alternative&#39;s crux: Heng Yuan Zhou requires the author to write laws to death before starting to write. Once laws are written to death, plot can only dance within the laws — this is not restricting creativity, but protecting creativity.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Tang-Luo system&#39;s three most-likely-kidnapped iron laws</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: simulate late plot needing breakthrough</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: after kidnapping occurs, law-authority drop magnitude</li><li><strong>Review conclusion</strong>: every kidnapping drops law authority about 15-20%; three kidnappings, laws basically invalid</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-high</strong></li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong></li><li><strong>Kidnapping risk points</strong>: fierce-realm cap, racial boundaries, top-tier knowledge private</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: law authority and reader trust repeatedly overdrawn</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: plot kidnapping = predation on reader intelligence</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo system&#39;s kidnapping risk points are precisely the structural defects repeatedly pointed out in the first 34 entries of this series</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: laws not kidnapped, 99%&#39;s situation does not stretch with plot</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: law-first is the cross-plane narrative bottom line</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="supplementary-discussion-priority-of-plot-and-law" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Discussion: Priority of Plot and Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-discussion-priority-of-plot-and-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Discussion: Priority of Plot and Law&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang-Luo system&#39;s sacrificing-law-for-plot cases are essentially plot kidnapping setting. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-first axiom expressly stipulates: law above plot. Plot can be twisty, can reverse, but cannot modify anchored laws for plot effect. The Alaya Network conducts compliance review on every plot-driven setting change; the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s creators and protagonists must narrate within the law framework. The universal equal infinite law is the bottom line not modifiable by plot; any operation that &quot;for tragic effect&quot; sacrifices Myriad Races rights is auto-blocked by the system.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Plot kidnapping setting is the chronic disease of long web novels. The Tang-Luo system is still early, kidnapping has not yet occurred at scale; but its single-point dependency structure is destined to face the &quot;kidnap or not&quot; dilemma late. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-first axiom is the only vaccine — write laws to death first, let plot dance within the laws.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · cases of plot kidnapping setting described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./97-设定矛盾自查表.html">97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table</a> · <a href="./90-术语词典.html">90-Glossary</a> · <a href="./98-扩展设定建议清单.html">98-Expanded Setting Recommendation List</a></li></ul>',33)])])}const u=t(o,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,u as default};
